WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.046
(audience cheering)

00:00:02.046 --> 00:00:02.879
- Green too!

00:00:02.879 --> 00:00:04.770
I was like, so green's my favorite color.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:05.603
- Well, good.

00:00:05.603 --> 00:00:07.840
- Yeah, my favorite color to wear is red.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.060
What's your favorite color to wear?

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:10.120
- Blue.
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:12.060
- But I'm a jewel tone girl.
- I'm a jewel tone girl.

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:13.440
- I go jewel tone.
- Yes.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.260
- All the pastels, I love
the idea of a pastel.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.340
- I don't, I look dead.
- Not good.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:18.670
- Yeah.
- Not good for me.

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:20.650
- I look dead, no matter how
much makeup you put on me.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:22.700
- Christmas, good, Easter, eh.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:24.920
- [Kelly] Yeah I don't do
Easter like that, yeah.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:25.870
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:27.690
- I'm glad we solved this.
- We did.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.570
- Crisis averted for the day.
- [Laura] I know.

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:31.225
- So you grew up in New York?
- I did.

00:00:31.225 --> 00:00:33.530
- It's such a great music scene there.

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:34.363
- It is.

00:00:34.363 --> 00:00:35.196
- I've seen so many amazing shows,

00:00:35.196 --> 00:00:36.270
be it like a small little club,

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:38.090
or a huge show at like the arena,

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:40.250
so what's like some of your best memories,

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:41.220
like music, where would you go?

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:42.360
- Well, we would go to the Garden.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.540
When I was growing up, it
would be Madison Square Garden.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:46.470
I saw the Beach Boys there.
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:49.320
- I took my sister to
a Duran Duran concert

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:50.467
and I saw Stevie Wonder there as well.

00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:52.710
- You saw Stevie Wonder?
- Yeah.

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:53.543
- [Kelly] I've never seen Stevie Wonder.

00:00:53.543 --> 00:00:54.910
- Well, listen, I have
to say there's one thing

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:56.547
I wanna tell you.

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:00.860
Because you did a song on the
"Love Actually" soundtrack--

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:01.693
- Yes.

00:01:01.693 --> 00:01:02.584
- Which is so beautiful, by the way.

00:01:02.584 --> 00:01:03.417
- "Trouble With Love" is--

00:01:03.417 --> 00:01:04.490
- It's a beautiful song.

00:01:04.490 --> 00:01:05.323
- Oh, thank you.

00:01:05.323 --> 00:01:06.955
Forget the song, I love the movie.

00:01:06.955 --> 00:01:07.788
(laughs)

00:01:07.788 --> 00:01:10.530
- But I almost met you on the red carpet.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:11.840
- What?
- For the premiere.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:15.690
We were there, you were
four people to the right.

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:16.940
And I couldn't get to you.

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:19.217
And it drove me crazy.
- What!

00:01:19.217 --> 00:01:20.760
You were trying to get to me?

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:22.650
- I was and here's why, here's why,

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:25.210
because I had this amazing
friend named Stanley DeSantis.

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:26.390
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:28.650
- Who was in a TV show called
"Tales the City" with me.

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:29.483
- Yeah.

00:01:29.483 --> 00:01:30.843
- We watched you every
week on "American Idol".

00:01:30.843 --> 00:01:31.676
- What!

00:01:31.676 --> 00:01:34.230
- We rooted for you
from the very beginning.

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:35.428
- What is happening?

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:36.600
(audience cheers)

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:37.600
Are you serious?

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:39.440
- We would call each other.

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:41.560
He lived in Los Angeles,
I lived in New York.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:44.460
It was like our thing was to watch you.

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:46.149
And you did a 40s song at one point.

00:01:46.149 --> 00:01:46.982
- That's my favorite one!

00:01:46.982 --> 00:01:48.890
- And we were like, "look at her go!"

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:50.651
Girl got range.
- Oh my God.

00:01:50.651 --> 00:01:51.680
- I mean, we were all over it.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:54.680
And he's no longer with
us, my friend Stanley.

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:57.200
But every time I see you, I think of him.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.033
- [Kelly] Ah, we love Stanley.

00:01:58.033 --> 00:02:00.670
- And so it's...
(audience clapping)

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:01.820
- I can't even believe-

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:04.700
- So you mean more than you ever knew.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:07.900
- That is the craziest
thing ever and so sweet.

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:10.100
But by the way, I
remember that red carpet.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.370
- Yeah, it was intense wasn't it?

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:12.203
- It was.

00:02:12.203 --> 00:02:16.518
And I had to go after Keira Knightley.

00:02:16.518 --> 00:02:18.933
- Oh yeah.
(laughs)

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:23.170
- And it's like red carpets
were still fairly new to me.

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:25.260
- I was thinking it must have
been one of your first ones.

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:28.030
- And she was like full on like a model.

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:29.973
- [Laura] Oh yeah.
- 'Cause she was just posing.

00:02:29.973 --> 00:02:31.750
- The girls know how to do it, I don't.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:33.010
- I looked like a girl scout.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:34.297
- I know you're like, "hi!"

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:37.820
- Right after Keira
Knightley, like I was like,

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:38.653
I tried so hard.

00:02:38.653 --> 00:02:40.883
And then I saw her like
posing and I was like, oh.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:44.230
I was like, I was trying.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.710
I felt so uncomfortable 'cause
I'm never around actors.

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:47.790
I'm always around musicians.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:50.360
- Sure, but I remember leaning back

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:52.010
and looking and seeing you.

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:54.460
- What!
- Like four people down

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:57.990
and I could never get
to you and I was so...

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:59.891
So here we are, 20 years later.

00:02:59.891 --> 00:03:01.667
- You would've made feel so good.

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:02.850
(audience clapping)
That's amazing.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:03.850
I have to say this though.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.960
So your friends are different from mine

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:07.500
because you shared this photo

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.260
of you and Brooke Shields as girls.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:10.130
Y'all knew each other as young kids?

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:11.510
- Isn't that funny?

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:12.343
Isn't that funny?

00:03:12.343 --> 00:03:13.710
We grew up together.
- What?

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:14.910
- Isn't that wild?
- Yes.

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:16.730
- I know we were in grade school together

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:18.700
and we were very close
for a period of time.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:19.533
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:03:19.533 --> 00:03:20.640
- And this was on a vacation.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:24.150
We went to Howe Caverns
together in upstate New York.

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:26.050
- I remember when that picture was taken.

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:28.320
And we have a very sweet friendship

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:31.390
because we've known each
other our entire lives.

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:33.010
We're not in contact all the time

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:34.970
but when we run into
each other occasionally

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:35.900
it's always so nice.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:36.950
'Cause we knew each other as--

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.108
- I have those friends that you've known

00:03:38.108 --> 00:03:39.270
since you were a kid.
- As little children.

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:41.300
I remember the stuffed animals on her bed.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:45.250
She remembers parents
who are no longer alive.

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:46.980
We have a deep connection that way.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:48.750
- That's so cool to have that kind of,

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:50.420
especially with you both
being in the limelight

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:51.660
and just being able to
talk about that as well.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:52.493
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:03:52.493 --> 00:03:54.270
No, that comes in very handy.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:55.440
- You have to have the safe people.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:56.470
- I just thought that was so random.

00:03:56.470 --> 00:03:57.303
I was like, wait, what?

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:58.462
- [Laura] Isn't that wild?
- Yes.

00:03:58.462 --> 00:03:59.346
- [Laura] I know.

00:03:59.346 --> 00:04:02.000
- I was like, your childhood
was different than mine.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.030
- Well I didn't go to
school with a dozen celebs.

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:06.536
- I know, I was like,
wow, that's so random.

00:04:06.536 --> 00:04:09.980
But your son is about that
age now, so how's he doing?

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:10.813
What's he into?

00:04:10.813 --> 00:04:12.050
- He's good, sports.
- Sports?

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:13.570
- Sports, sports, sports, sports, sports.

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:14.970
- Sports ball.

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:16.350
- Anything with a ball that you run.

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:18.140
- [Kelly] My daughter's like that.

00:04:18.140 --> 00:04:21.750
- Football, basketball,
Chicago Bulls, Brooklyn Nets.

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:22.583
The whole thing.

00:04:22.583 --> 00:04:24.060
- That's amazing, my
daughter's really into sports,

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:26.282
my son is into like Legos.

00:04:26.282 --> 00:04:28.090
- [Laura] Oh yes, yeah, isn't that fun?

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:29.727
- Anything built, he
loves to build anything.

00:04:29.727 --> 00:04:30.950
- I like the Legos.

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:32.647
- [Kelly] I know, but I love it.

00:04:32.647 --> 00:04:33.960
- Oh my God, I love it too,
but there's so many of them.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:34.840
- [Kelly] I know, but I love it.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:36.540
- Oh my God, and then
you gotta organize them

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:37.373
and the whole thing.

00:04:37.373 --> 00:04:39.870
- Because you can check out
and the directions are so,

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:42.210
It's kind of therapeutic
- I love the directions.

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:44.510
- I feel like people
that put those directions

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:47.023
like together for Legos
should do that for furniture,

00:04:47.023 --> 00:04:48.550
whoever does that.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:51.357
'Cause they're way better
at it than the other people.

00:04:51.357 --> 00:04:53.480
- But I want like Lego socks

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:55.799
so that when I step on them, I don't,

00:04:55.799 --> 00:04:58.309
(audience laughs)
I want like a special sock.

00:04:58.309 --> 00:05:00.365
(audience claps)

00:05:00.365 --> 00:05:01.630
- So I'm a disciplinary.

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:02.730
So like I'm that mom.

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:04.777
So like we don't have many
Legos hanging out on the floor.

00:05:04.777 --> 00:05:05.880
- You see, I would--

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:08.320
- [Kelly] I throw them away
- Come to my house.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:09.230
Can you come help me out?

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:10.090
- I'm this mom.

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:11.770
I literally don't care if I bought it.

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:13.280
I will be like, if it's not gone

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:15.290
by the time I walk back through this room,

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:17.330
and they know, it'll go
directly in the trash.

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:18.163
- [Laura] Good for you.

00:05:18.163 --> 00:05:21.040
- Yeah, 'cause I am not a broken record.

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:22.787
I don't like repeating myself constantly.

00:05:22.787 --> 00:05:25.328
- Well and they're at that age now.

00:05:25.328 --> 00:05:28.230
- I don't know how many times
to tell you to pick that up.

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:29.220
So I'm just gonna throw it away.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:31.003
- You need to come to my house.

00:05:32.039 --> 00:05:32.872
(audience cheers)

00:05:32.872 --> 00:05:34.810
- That was a clip from
her Netflix series "Ozark".

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:37.410
It's amazing!

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:39.190
But we have a tradition around here

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:42.500
where a Bundt cake a pan is
passed from person to person

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:43.860
on the staff and crew each week.

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:45.740
And basically you pass the pan

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:48.240
to someone who you appreciate
and you wanna thank

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:51.890
but you have to do it as
a surprise or a prank.

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:52.843
I prefer prank.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:55.256
By saying like, "you've been bunted."

00:05:55.256 --> 00:05:58.010
So when the person you're
bunting, they least expect it.

00:05:58.010 --> 00:05:58.990
So you kind of get freaked out.

00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:01.310
So then that person has to make a cake.

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:03.300
So I hear that you are into Bundts.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:04.640
- I Bundt.

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:06.300
- [Kelly] You Bundt, you Bundt.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:07.390
- I have been known to Bundt.

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:08.890
- [Kelly] What's your favorite Bundt?

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:10.010
- Coca-Cola Bundt.

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:10.843
- Wait, what?

00:06:10.843 --> 00:06:12.240
- [Laura] Yeah, Coca-Cola Bundt cake.

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:13.803
- You just mixed a soft drink with a cake.

00:06:13.803 --> 00:06:15.502
- Yes, I sure did.
- [Kelly] I like that.

00:06:15.502 --> 00:06:16.650
- But actually the people
who do it the best,

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:19.180
there's a bakery in New
York City called Baked.

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:21.972
They make a Coca-Cola Bundt
cake that is like no other.

00:06:21.972 --> 00:06:23.964
- There's a lot of stores
here in LA named Baked.

00:06:23.964 --> 00:06:26.730
(laughs)
- Different kind.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:27.720
- But actually I brought one.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.698
- You brought one! (gasps)

00:06:29.698 --> 00:06:31.126
(audience cheers)

00:06:31.126 --> 00:06:32.640
- I'm so excited, I've never heard of a--

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:33.910
- Oh, it's so good.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:35.810
- Can we just, you know,
what's great about a Bundt?

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:37.744
It's so moist if it's done right.

00:06:37.744 --> 00:06:38.630
- Oh, well wait.

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:40.420
- Okay, I'm just taking a butt.

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:41.920
Oh, they gave us one.

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:43.180
Oh wait, here's your--

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:44.810
Look we're passing to each other.

00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:46.880
Okay wait, did you smell that?

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:48.420
Did you smell that?

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:49.509
You can't smell that, but I did.

00:06:49.509 --> 00:06:53.463
Oh my God, this is gonna be good.

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:57.133
- Come on.

00:06:58.270 --> 00:06:59.533
Come on.
- Oh my God.

00:07:00.537 --> 00:07:01.370
- How about that?

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:02.280
- I love cake.

00:07:03.262 --> 00:07:04.490
- Isn't it good?

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:05.323
- Oh my gosh.

00:07:05.323 --> 00:07:06.570
Oh my gosh.
- You're welcome.

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:09.660
- So I have to, I wanted to
get to that 'cause I smelled it

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:11.610
and that's why I cut to that after Ozark.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:13.860
But I find this amazing
'cause you're one of the,

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:15.180
it's an amazing cast.

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:16.060
It's so well done.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:18.290
But it's when I watch you, it's just like,

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:20.130
I know it's gonna sound like
such a tool thing to say,

00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:24.482
but you're like one of the
like true really great actors.

00:07:24.482 --> 00:07:25.474
- That's very kind.
(audience claps)

00:07:25.474 --> 00:07:26.307
- And it's funny to me

00:07:26.307 --> 00:07:29.709
because you had like
stagefright starting out.

00:07:29.709 --> 00:07:30.542
- Oh yeah.

00:07:30.542 --> 00:07:34.100
- I can never picture someone
as talented as you afraid.

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:35.610
- Oh, no, no, absolutely, absolutely.

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:36.443
- That's so--

00:07:36.443 --> 00:07:38.530
- I mean, most of us are
nervous all the time.

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:39.680
You know, it's just human nature.

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:41.360
It's not a natural thing to do.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:43.490
- I'm not in singing.
- Which is unbelievable.

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:45.980
- But in acting--
- I can't sing.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:48.520
In my next life, I'm a
musical theater person

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:51.441
but no one wants to hear me sing.

00:07:51.441 --> 00:07:52.970
- How did you get over that?

00:07:52.970 --> 00:07:54.097
'Cause you're so good.

00:07:54.097 --> 00:07:57.120
- I was able to go to
Juilliard for graduate school,

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:58.920
which was an amazing experience.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:01.990
And during my third year
there, I completely fell apart.

00:08:01.990 --> 00:08:04.870
And I developed a stage
fright that was just brutal.

00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:06.550
It was awful.
- Did something happen?

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:08.700
- I did a play that just broke me.

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:12.120
And I just got scared and
I didn't wanna be there

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:13.860
and I almost dropped out of school.

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:14.989
- Oh my God.

00:08:14.989 --> 00:08:16.760
- I got to point I was
like, this is too hard.

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:18.719
I can't do this, this is ridiculous.

00:08:18.719 --> 00:08:21.810
And I had a wonderful teacher
by the name of John Sticks

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:23.127
who pulled me aside and he said,

00:08:23.127 --> 00:08:25.417
"look, this is where you fail.

00:08:25.417 --> 00:08:27.850
"This is where you have to fail."

00:08:27.850 --> 00:08:29.095
- Oh, this is where you're
supposed to be learning.

00:08:29.095 --> 00:08:30.287
- He's like, "this is where
you're supposed to fail

00:08:30.287 --> 00:08:33.620
"is here, so good, congratulations."

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:36.810
He's like, "you must fail
in order to get better."

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:38.430
And it was a great lesson.
- Yeah.

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:40.380
- And like the big lesson always for me

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:42.380
is how to learn to sit in discomfort

00:08:42.380 --> 00:08:45.143
and let things catch up
until you can move out of it.

00:08:45.143 --> 00:08:48.869
- This is why I'm not an actor
'cause I avoid the (bleep)--

00:08:48.869 --> 00:08:50.000
(audience laughs)

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:51.400
- But you know how to tell a story

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:52.740
so you can feel the narrative,

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:54.490
you can feel suspense within the music.

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:55.930
- I guess I've never thought
of it as like a song.

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:57.480
- The rhythm and the timing

00:08:57.480 --> 00:08:59.160
and that you can feel when things are,

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:01.126
you know, you craft things in a way that

00:09:01.126 --> 00:09:04.545
maybe you're not even
aware of, but it's similar.

00:09:04.545 --> 00:09:06.120
- I don't know.

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:07.570
I think you just told me that I'm you.

00:09:07.570 --> 00:09:09.500
So I'm gonna take that and (laughs)

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:11.989
I'm gonna filter that as I'm
talented, like Laura Linney.

00:09:11.989 --> 00:09:15.590
Are you satisfied with the ending?

00:09:15.590 --> 00:09:17.430
'Cause when there's such
a huge show like this

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:19.247
that hits in pop culture
that everybody loves.

00:09:19.247 --> 00:09:20.080
Do you get nervous?

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:22.910
- I am, I wish it would go on forever.

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:25.640
So I wouldn't be satisfied with any ending

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:27.130
'cause I'm just gonna miss it so much.

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:28.000
But yes.
- [Kelly] Oh, I love that.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.490
- [Laura] Yes, they did
a wonderful job with it.

00:09:30.490 --> 00:09:31.840
- [Kelly] Not everybody
loves their show like that.

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:33.410
- I know we're very lucky.

00:09:33.410 --> 00:09:35.710
It was a wonderful
experience for all of us.

00:09:35.710 --> 00:09:38.070
We all loved it so I'm
just very sad it's ending.

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:39.980
- Do you think the fans
are gonna freak out

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:41.800
in a good way or bad way?

00:09:41.800 --> 00:09:42.633
- I don't know.

00:09:42.633 --> 00:09:44.363
I really, I have no idea.

00:09:44.363 --> 00:09:48.070
But I think they'll freak out

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:49.700
- What a great tease!

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:51.110
Okay, I love that.

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:53.740
So the show is about what
people will do to survive.

00:09:53.740 --> 00:09:55.380
So how do you think that you'd do

00:09:55.380 --> 00:09:57.440
with the FBI and the cartel on you?

00:09:57.440 --> 00:09:58.833
- Oh, I'm such a good girl.

00:09:58.833 --> 00:10:00.156
- [Kelly] I am too.
- I'm so square.

00:10:00.156 --> 00:10:01.440
- [Kelly] I'm not exciting.
I'm square I'm not.

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:02.337
I'm boring and square
- [Kelly] Me too.

00:10:02.337 --> 00:10:03.420
- And always have been.

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:05.520
- Yeah, I like try and think
I'm really cool, I'm not.

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:08.779
- I got a speeding ticket a few years ago.

00:10:08.779 --> 00:10:09.612
- [Kelly] I love that
that's your bad thing.

00:10:09.612 --> 00:10:10.562
- That's my bad,

00:10:10.562 --> 00:10:11.787
I got a speeding ticket and they came,

00:10:11.787 --> 00:10:13.540
"Well, you know you're speeding?"

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:15.760
I was like, "Yeah, I am, I'm
so sorry, give me the ticket."

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:16.630
- Oh my God I'd do that.

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:17.640
- Yeah, I'm like you're right.

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:19.465
I didn't realize.
- Yeah.

00:10:19.465 --> 00:10:20.760
You're probably gonna
give it to me anyway,

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:21.593
so let's just, you know.

00:10:21.593 --> 00:10:22.490
- Let's just get it over with.

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:24.050
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- I'm so sorry, mea culpa.

00:10:24.050 --> 00:10:25.290
- But that's your bad
thing though is speeding.

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:27.060
That's amazing.
- Yeah that's it

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:28.435
I'm boring, I'm so dull.

00:10:28.435 --> 00:10:29.283
- (laughs) Freaking rebel.

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:32.840
All right, so we need another break.

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:35.993
- Okay, this is, can I do this now?

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:39.280
Your staff has been so kind.

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:40.113
- Thank you.

00:10:40.113 --> 00:10:41.480
- [Laura] Your staff has been
really, really wonderful.

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:42.670
- I love my staff.
(audience clapping)

00:10:42.670 --> 00:10:46.960
- And particularly I
wanna thank your IT guy.

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:47.980
- [Kelly] Tito?
- Tito.

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:48.813
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:10:48.813 --> 00:10:50.720
- Who helped me sort of, with my phone

00:10:50.720 --> 00:10:51.820
before we came out or so.

00:10:51.820 --> 00:10:52.653
Is he around?

00:10:52.653 --> 00:10:54.934
- Are you giving Tito a shout right now?

00:10:54.934 --> 00:10:55.767
- [Laura] I'm giving Tito a shout out.

00:10:55.767 --> 00:10:58.620
- Wait, Tito, Laura Linney just asked

00:10:58.620 --> 00:11:01.010
for you to come down here.

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:04.253
Hey, what's up Tito?
(audience cheering)

00:11:04.253 --> 00:11:05.608
There he is!

00:11:05.608 --> 00:11:08.130
So Laura wanted to thank
you for making sure

00:11:08.130 --> 00:11:09.143
that her Internet connection was--

00:11:09.143 --> 00:11:11.860
- I just wanted to thank
you very, very much

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:12.790
for all of your help.

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:14.790
I know you came in and, you know,

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:18.110
get my phone secure and all of that.

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:19.737
- That's for you, Tito.

00:11:19.737 --> 00:11:21.787
She's miced! (laughs)
- That's your mic.

00:11:22.890 --> 00:11:25.770
- I think I know what's gonna happen next.

00:11:25.770 --> 00:11:29.130
- So I just wanna say
from me and everyone here,

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:30.453
you've been Bundted.

00:11:30.453 --> 00:11:35.453
- Yay!
(audience cheers)

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:39.565
That is right, Tito.

00:11:39.565 --> 00:11:41.793
And a special shout out from Andra who,

00:11:41.793 --> 00:11:43.400
along with everybody here,

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:45.220
thanks you for giving us all peace of mind

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:47.850
while we shop online when
we're supposed to be working

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:49.240
and Laura Linney just bunted you too.

00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:50.610
That's amazing.

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:53.484
- Thank you, Andra.
- It's so amazing! (laughs)

00:11:53.484 --> 00:11:57.584
I love that you were
like, "Ma'am?" (laughs)

00:11:57.584 --> 00:12:01.250
Tito, she's got a mic on. (laughs)

00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:02.970
You are so awesome for doing that.

